>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `LINARITH_TAC`

``` hol4
linarithLib.LINARITH_TAC : thm list -> tactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Proves a goal using full linear-arithmetic preprocessing and certificate
replay.

`LINARITH_TAC thms` is
`CFG_LINARITH_TAC linarithLib.default_config thms`. It inserts persistent
`[arith]` facts and each unmarked theorem in `thms`, negates the
conclusion, filters irrelevant assumptions, converts Boolean structure to
negation normal form, repeatedly applies operator-splitting rules, adds
applicable division and modulus facts, and refutes every resulting linear
constraint system.

The split corpus consists of persistent `[arith_split]` declarations,
per-instance rules, and arguments marked `markerLib.Split th`. Classical,
simplifier, and Iff markers are rejected. The default `neq_limit` and
`split_limit` are both 9. The tactic has close-or-fail semantics.

### Failure

Fails if preprocessing or linear arithmetic does not close every goal, if
a needed carrier has no registered instance, if a limit is exceeded, or
if an argument has an unsupported marker. A malformed split theorem is
also rejected.

### Example

``` hol4
Theorem linarith_tac_example:
  !m n : num. MIN m n <= m
Proof
  rpt strip_tac >>
  linarithLib.LINARITH_TAC []
QED
```

